  "body": "Part of #2007.\n\nMaintainer in chat, 2026-11-15: \"That tool editor issue is a P3\". The issue quotes: \"a weldon is a weldon\".\n\n## What happens\n\n`crates/tools/src/holder_library.rs` has one Weldon entry for each bore and each taper. `Clamp::Weldon{bore, body_d}` is repeated for `METRIC_BORES` 6/8/10/12/16/20 and `INCH_BORES` (L286-296) in `library()` (L306-341). The picker thus lists many Weldon entries.\n\n## What to do\n\n- Show one \"Weldon\" entry for each taper in the holder picker (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tool_holder_picker.rs`).\n- Take the bore and the body diameter from the standard bore table by the tool's shank diameter.\n- Refuse a shank with no standard bore by name. Use the existing `LibraryError::Shank` text of `fits_shank` (L220-229).\n- Keep one bore for each holder in the data. A real Weldon holder has a fixed bore. Only the picker and the reference change.\n\nThe body diameter is a collision shape: `effort:high` by the safety floor.\n\n## Done means:\n\n- The picker shows one Weldon entry for each taper.\n- A tool with a 10 mm shank gets the 10 mm bore and its body diameter. A test pins this.\n- A shank with no standard bore is refused by name. A test pins the message.\n- The collision bands of a picked Weldon holder are the same as those of the old bore entry. A test pins this.\n\nOrder: after the holder reference sub-issue.\n",
